1
00:01:38,020 --> 00:01:43,940
[Small Town Remedy]

2
00:01:44,220 --> 00:01:46,820
[Episode 3]

3
00:01:49,789 --> 00:01:50,720
Liu Zhengliang.

4
00:01:51,310 --> 00:01:52,430
What kind of place do you think

5
00:01:52,430 --> 00:01:53,759
Xiaoximen Hospital is?

6
00:01:53,950 --> 00:01:55,840
One you can just come and go?

7
00:01:57,120 --> 00:01:58,400
Didn't we agree?

8
00:01:58,870 --> 00:02:00,200
Once Liu Zhengguang's surgery is over,

9
00:02:00,200 --> 00:02:01,000
I'll leave.

10
00:02:01,120 --> 00:02:02,580
Have you lost your memory?

11
00:02:03,150 --> 00:02:04,150
We agreed you'd stay

12
00:02:04,150 --> 00:02:05,400
at Xiaoximen Hospital.

13
00:02:05,400 --> 00:02:06,680
You raised the price,

14
00:02:06,680 --> 00:02:08,139
and I reluctantly agreed.

15
00:02:09,470 --> 00:02:10,310
Who'd want to stay at a hospital

16
00:02:10,310 --> 00:02:11,710
where the director barbecues in his office

17
00:02:11,710 --> 00:02:13,150
in broad daylight?

18
00:02:16,430 --> 00:02:18,400
Then what about the contract you signed?

19
00:02:18,400 --> 00:02:19,079
No problem.

20
00:02:19,360 --> 00:02:20,630
I can pay the penalty.

21
00:02:28,310 --> 00:02:30,030
WeChat or cash, either works.

22
00:02:32,150 --> 00:02:33,560
Can I pay in installments?

23
00:02:33,560 --> 00:02:34,590
Never heard of that.

24
00:02:34,590 --> 00:02:35,030
Around here,

25
00:02:35,030 --> 00:02:36,120
we only do one-time deals.

26
00:02:36,120 --> 00:02:37,150
What do you mean?

27
00:02:37,240 --> 00:02:38,280
Are you in the mob?

28
00:02:38,710 --> 00:02:39,520
Let me tell you,

29
00:02:39,520 --> 00:02:41,310
we live under the rule of law.

30
00:02:41,630 --> 00:02:43,079
Even if I insist on going,

31
00:02:43,079 --> 00:02:44,240
what can you do about it?

32
00:02:44,240 --> 00:02:45,500
Tie me up or something?

33
00:02:46,870 --> 00:02:47,750
What?

34
00:02:48,840 --> 00:02:50,400
You think running back to Guangdong

35
00:02:50,400 --> 00:02:52,000
will put you beyond my reach?

36
00:02:52,710 --> 00:02:54,590
I've got connections in Guangdong too.

37
00:02:54,590 --> 00:02:57,790
My classmate heads
the South China Medical Association.

38
00:02:58,120 --> 00:02:59,870
I'll spread the word

39
00:03:00,190 --> 00:03:01,910
about your malpractice and unpaid debts.

40
00:03:01,910 --> 00:03:02,840
How do you like that?

41
00:03:02,840 --> 00:03:04,770
What hospital would hire you then?

42
00:03:06,470 --> 00:03:07,360
I'm sick!

43
00:03:07,360 --> 00:03:08,240
You? Sick?

44
00:03:08,710 --> 00:03:09,430
I mean it. I'm sick.

45
00:03:09,430 --> 00:03:10,240
I'm really sick.

46
00:03:10,240 --> 00:03:12,840
I'm scared of snow
(sounds like "blood" in Chinese).

47
00:03:12,840 --> 00:03:13,470
What?

48
00:03:14,030 --> 00:03:14,910
You don't see blood during brain surgery?

49
00:03:14,910 --> 00:03:16,150
Not that kind of blood.

50
00:03:16,150 --> 00:03:17,350
Snow, as in snowfall.

51
00:03:18,120 --> 00:03:19,430
The stuff that comes fluttering down

52
00:03:19,430 --> 00:03:20,240
from the sky.

53
00:03:20,750 --> 00:03:21,710
Snow phobia?

54
00:03:25,400 --> 00:03:27,060
You're really pulling my leg.

55
00:03:27,520 --> 00:03:29,120
I've been a doctor for years,

56
00:03:29,400 --> 00:03:31,000
and I've never heard of that condition.

57
00:03:31,000 --> 00:03:32,840
Look it up if you don't believe me.

58
00:03:32,840 --> 00:03:33,710
Chionophobia

59
00:03:33,910 --> 00:03:35,310
is a rare condition.

60
00:03:35,360 --> 00:03:36,280
Most sufferers have experienced

61
00:03:36,280 --> 00:03:37,470
a serious accident

62
00:03:37,520 --> 00:03:38,710
on a snowy day.

63
00:03:38,750 --> 00:03:39,680
Just like me.

64
00:03:39,960 --> 00:03:41,030
When I see snow,

65
00:03:41,079 --> 00:03:42,470
I feel disgusted

66
00:03:42,470 --> 00:03:44,360
and have panic attacks.

67
00:03:44,680 --> 00:03:45,710
I even experience

68
00:03:46,079 --> 00:03:47,910
severe physical symptoms.

69
00:03:47,910 --> 00:03:49,030
I get a rapid heartbeat

70
00:03:49,030 --> 00:03:50,400
and shortness of breath.

71
00:03:50,400 --> 00:03:51,240
I even feel

72
00:03:51,240 --> 00:03:52,120
like I'm suffocating,

73
00:03:52,120 --> 00:03:52,800
like I'm about to die...

74
00:03:52,800 --> 00:03:53,400
What's that got to do

75
00:03:53,400 --> 00:03:54,280
with you staying?

76
00:03:54,280 --> 00:03:55,520
It snows here!

77
00:03:55,870 --> 00:03:57,130
I have to go back south.

78
00:03:57,520 --> 00:03:58,120
Oh, right.

79
00:03:58,800 --> 00:03:59,660
Now I remember.

80
00:04:01,030 --> 00:04:02,120
You were covering your eyes

81
00:04:02,120 --> 00:04:03,150
last time.

82
00:04:03,190 --> 00:04:04,590
So you're afraid of snow.

83
00:04:07,360 --> 00:04:08,160
That's right.

84
00:04:08,840 --> 00:04:10,080
I grew up in the Northeast.

85
00:04:10,080 --> 00:04:11,630
Whenever it snowed in winter,

86
00:04:11,630 --> 00:04:13,160
I couldn't even go outside.

87
00:04:15,400 --> 00:04:16,329
Liu Zhengliang,

88
00:04:17,160 --> 00:04:18,360
you're not making this up, are you?

89
00:04:18,360 --> 00:04:19,600
I swear I'm not.

90
00:04:19,950 --> 00:04:21,480
Because of this condition,

91
00:04:24,560 --> 00:04:26,040
my mom sent me away

92
00:04:26,360 --> 00:04:27,360
when I was little.

93
00:04:39,070 --> 00:04:39,670
All right.

94
00:04:40,630 --> 00:04:41,680
I buy it.

95
00:04:45,720 --> 00:04:46,390
Thanks.

96
00:04:49,000 --> 00:04:49,630
Your condition

97
00:04:49,630 --> 00:04:51,290
is the mildest I've ever seen.

98
00:04:51,600 --> 00:04:53,000
Now I've got something else

99
00:04:53,000 --> 00:04:54,060
to use against you.

100
00:05:09,630 --> 00:05:10,630
Darn it.

101
00:05:11,340 --> 00:05:13,460
[Outpatient Clinic]

102
00:05:14,560 --> 00:05:15,160
Right.

103
00:05:15,160 --> 00:05:16,190
Who's this?

104
00:05:16,800 --> 00:05:17,920
This is a senior official
from the Health Commission,

105
00:05:17,920 --> 00:05:18,310
Junnan!

106
00:05:18,310 --> 00:05:19,600
Nice to see you!

107
00:05:19,600 --> 00:05:20,070
Come on, this way.

108
00:05:20,070 --> 00:05:21,120
I reckon Dr. Chen

109
00:05:21,120 --> 00:05:23,050
will be Director Chen before long.

110
00:05:23,720 --> 00:05:25,240
He was just born lucky.

111
00:05:26,120 --> 00:05:27,630
A promising young man indeed.

112
00:05:27,630 --> 00:05:29,510
I'm quite envious.

113
00:05:31,680 --> 00:05:33,000
All right, Director Liu.

114
00:05:33,000 --> 00:05:33,720
Thank you.

115
00:05:33,720 --> 00:05:35,070
You came all this way in person.

116
00:05:35,070 --> 00:05:36,040
Thank you so much.

117
00:05:36,040 --> 00:05:36,480
All right.

118
00:05:36,480 --> 00:05:37,070
Okay.

119
00:05:37,070 --> 00:05:37,800
Take care.

120
00:05:37,800 --> 00:05:38,600
This way.

121
00:05:38,720 --> 00:05:40,920
We look forward to your guidance again.

122
00:05:42,240 --> 00:05:43,240
This way, please.

123
00:05:46,000 --> 00:05:46,720
What brings you here?

124
00:05:46,720 --> 00:05:47,580
I'm in trouble.

125
00:05:47,830 --> 00:05:48,510
What happened?

126
00:05:48,510 --> 00:05:50,240
You can't go even after you pay?

127
00:05:50,630 --> 00:05:52,290
They've taken a liking to you.

128
00:05:52,870 --> 00:05:53,600
Back then,

129
00:05:53,600 --> 00:05:54,870
I shouldn't have saved him.

130
00:05:54,870 --> 00:05:56,800
I should've let you just trach him.

131
00:05:57,000 --> 00:05:57,680
He'd probably still

132
00:05:57,680 --> 00:05:58,940
be at home recovering.

133
00:05:59,000 --> 00:06:00,390
That's not fair.

134
00:06:00,600 --> 00:06:02,190
Watch what you say.

135
00:06:02,510 --> 00:06:04,480
If you leave, what about Zhengguang?

136
00:06:04,480 --> 00:06:05,510
People in small towns

137
00:06:05,510 --> 00:06:06,480
are hopeless.

138
00:06:06,720 --> 00:06:08,480
They don't honor contracts at all.

139
00:06:08,480 --> 00:06:09,360
Now they're openly reneging.

140
00:06:09,360 --> 00:06:10,950
People in small towns?

141
00:06:10,970 --> 00:06:12,100
[Kindly close the door behind you]

142
00:06:12,920 --> 00:06:14,190
You're the one backing out.

143
00:06:14,190 --> 00:06:14,680
Besides,

144
00:06:14,680 --> 00:06:16,040
aren't you from a small town too?

145
00:06:16,040 --> 00:06:17,950
No, I'm from Shenzhen.

146
00:06:18,510 --> 00:06:19,360
That's why I can't get used

147
00:06:19,360 --> 00:06:20,690
to how things work here.

148
00:06:20,720 --> 00:06:21,240
Come on.

149
00:06:21,560 --> 00:06:23,830
Picking up a few Cantonese phrases,

150
00:06:24,070 --> 00:06:26,330
and you think you're a Guangdong native?

151
00:06:26,750 --> 00:06:28,550
You've barely been back a while,

152
00:06:30,560 --> 00:06:31,270
and your Northeastern accent

153
00:06:31,270 --> 00:06:32,600
is already coming back.

154
00:06:32,630 --> 00:06:33,510
Who says so?

155
00:06:33,720 --> 00:06:34,720
I don't have an accent.

156
00:06:34,720 --> 00:06:36,250
I speak standard Mandarin.

157
00:06:38,680 --> 00:06:40,040
Look at your accent.

158
00:06:40,040 --> 00:06:41,560
I don't have one.

159
00:06:41,800 --> 00:06:42,750
It's all your fault.

160
00:06:42,750 --> 00:06:43,750
Could you please speak

161
00:06:43,750 --> 00:06:44,830
standard Mandarin?

162
00:06:44,830 --> 00:06:46,159
It's all my fault?

163
00:06:46,270 --> 00:06:48,120
Next time I talk to you,

164
00:06:48,800 --> 00:06:50,000
I'll speak Mandarin.

165
00:06:51,510 --> 00:06:52,270
No way.

166
00:06:52,750 --> 00:06:54,750
I need to find a way out of here, fast.

167
00:06:55,430 --> 00:06:56,480
He even told me

168
00:06:56,480 --> 00:06:57,120
I'm the least sick person

169
00:06:57,120 --> 00:06:58,520
they've ever seen there.

170
00:07:00,160 --> 00:07:01,430
Do you think

171
00:07:01,800 --> 00:07:03,480
he's got some kind of weird fetish?

172
00:07:03,480 --> 00:07:04,870
I know Xiaoximen Hospital.

173
00:07:04,870 --> 00:07:06,270
They're short-staffed.

174
00:07:06,310 --> 00:07:07,190
He must think

175
00:07:07,190 --> 00:07:08,520
you're good at your job.

176
00:07:10,190 --> 00:07:11,190
That makes sense.

177
00:07:11,190 --> 00:07:11,870
Go on.

178
00:07:12,190 --> 00:07:13,070
If you really want out,

179
00:07:13,070 --> 00:07:14,070
I've got an idea.

180
00:07:15,310 --> 00:07:16,720
Why not just coast

181
00:07:16,830 --> 00:07:18,160
and do the bare minimum?

182
00:07:18,360 --> 00:07:19,190
You mean

183
00:07:19,190 --> 00:07:20,270
I should act incompetent

184
00:07:20,270 --> 00:07:21,480
until he fires me?

185
00:07:22,270 --> 00:07:23,070
Exactly.

186
00:07:25,040 --> 00:07:27,240
But I don't know how to act incompetent.

187
00:07:27,390 --> 00:07:28,920
It's hard to fake being a genius,

188
00:07:28,920 --> 00:07:30,630
but acting useless is easy.

189
00:07:31,230 --> 00:07:34,590
[Xiaoximen Hospital]

190
00:07:33,360 --> 00:07:34,240
Hey, Jia.

191
00:07:34,800 --> 00:07:35,560
Could you check

192
00:07:35,560 --> 00:07:36,920
with the fire department again?

193
00:07:36,920 --> 00:07:38,070
They've confirmed

194
00:07:38,070 --> 00:07:40,480
your mom isn't at that spot in the water.

195
00:07:40,480 --> 00:07:42,409
More days of searching won't help.

196
00:07:43,430 --> 00:07:44,360
Could they search

197
00:07:44,360 --> 00:07:45,190
farther downstream

198
00:07:45,190 --> 00:07:46,600
along the riverbank?

199
00:07:46,630 --> 00:07:49,600
They say she's not
in this stretch of river.

200
00:07:49,950 --> 00:07:50,870
What about the tributaries?

201
00:07:50,870 --> 00:07:52,120
They can't find her.

202
00:07:52,360 --> 00:07:54,680
Zhengguang, your brother is right.

203
00:07:54,870 --> 00:07:57,390
The current must've carried her away.

204
00:07:57,430 --> 00:07:59,310
Have you contacted
anyone near the river mouth?

205
00:07:59,310 --> 00:08:00,630
I just can't give up.

206
00:08:00,750 --> 00:08:01,870
Isn't there anything else we can do?

207
00:08:01,870 --> 00:08:03,750
Just give it a little more time, okay?

208
00:08:03,750 --> 00:08:04,950
All right. Thanks.

209
00:08:04,950 --> 00:08:06,410
I'll see what else I can do.

210
00:08:12,040 --> 00:08:13,720
Come on, let's eat.

211
00:08:18,040 --> 00:08:19,000
When are you going back to Shenzhen?

212
00:08:19,000 --> 00:08:20,070
Not anytime soon.

213
00:08:20,240 --> 00:08:21,430
I have to stay in this dump

214
00:08:21,430 --> 00:08:22,070
and work.

215
00:08:23,160 --> 00:08:24,240
Stay here and work?

216
00:08:24,480 --> 00:08:26,280
What about your job in Shenzhen?

217
00:08:27,430 --> 00:08:28,960
I don't work there anymore.

218
00:08:30,000 --> 00:08:31,630
Did you quit,

219
00:08:31,630 --> 00:08:33,120
or did they fire you?

220
00:08:33,960 --> 00:08:34,870
Stop prying.

221
00:08:35,390 --> 00:08:37,250
You wouldn't understand anyway.

222
00:08:37,360 --> 00:08:39,510
How is that prying?

223
00:08:40,080 --> 00:08:42,000
I bet you got fired.

224
00:08:43,200 --> 00:08:44,480
Let's be honest.

225
00:08:44,750 --> 00:08:46,120
With your personality,

226
00:08:46,630 --> 00:08:47,480
they were already being nice

227
00:08:47,480 --> 00:08:48,360
to keep you around

228
00:08:48,360 --> 00:08:50,030
for as long as they did.

229
00:08:50,750 --> 00:08:52,600
If this hospital won't keep you either,

230
00:08:52,600 --> 00:08:53,550
come with me.

231
00:08:55,030 --> 00:08:55,790
Take care.

232
00:08:55,790 --> 00:08:57,190
We'll sell funeral urns.

233
00:09:01,120 --> 00:09:01,840
Didn't you tell me

234
00:09:01,840 --> 00:09:03,700
you worked for a foreign company?

235
00:09:04,200 --> 00:09:05,080
Who said that?

236
00:09:06,320 --> 00:09:07,510
You did.

237
00:09:08,080 --> 00:09:09,200
The Dragon Boat Festival three years ago.

238
00:09:09,200 --> 00:09:12,000
I don't remember.
I must've been messing with you.

239
00:09:12,000 --> 00:09:12,750
Besides,

240
00:09:12,750 --> 00:09:13,390
what foreign company

241
00:09:13,390 --> 00:09:15,030
would hire a low-education guy like me?

242
00:09:15,030 --> 00:09:15,750
Actually,

243
00:09:15,960 --> 00:09:16,840
I should ask:

244
00:09:16,910 --> 00:09:19,390
what foreign companies
are there around here?

245
00:09:19,390 --> 00:09:21,480
You didn't really believe me, did you?

246
00:09:21,480 --> 00:09:22,150
Haven't you met

247
00:09:22,150 --> 00:09:23,680
my boss at the funeral home?

248
00:09:24,150 --> 00:09:24,910
Who?

249
00:09:26,030 --> 00:09:27,080
Ms. Aichen,

250
00:09:27,390 --> 00:09:29,720
the pretty, skinny lady,

251
00:09:29,720 --> 00:09:30,360
remember?

252
00:09:30,630 --> 00:09:31,510
Her?

253
00:09:31,510 --> 00:09:32,840
I thought she was your superior.

254
00:09:32,840 --> 00:09:34,080
Eat it while it's warm.

255
00:09:34,080 --> 00:09:35,140
She is my superior.

256
00:09:35,790 --> 00:09:37,590
But we're not a foreign company.

257
00:09:39,240 --> 00:09:40,640
It's a funeral business.

258
00:09:41,150 --> 00:09:42,680
A funeral service company.

259
00:09:42,790 --> 00:09:43,750
She gets up early every day

260
00:09:43,750 --> 00:09:45,410
and keeps a regular schedule.

261
00:09:50,790 --> 00:09:51,650
How about this?

262
00:09:52,120 --> 00:09:53,150
Once you're discharged,

263
00:09:53,150 --> 00:09:54,390
I'll help you find

264
00:09:54,550 --> 00:09:55,360
another job.

265
00:09:56,150 --> 00:09:56,910
Why?

266
00:09:57,510 --> 00:09:58,640
I'm doing just fine.

267
00:10:02,270 --> 00:10:03,470
Mom said in her letter

268
00:10:03,870 --> 00:10:04,930
to take care of you.

269
00:10:07,360 --> 00:10:08,390
What Mom meant was,

270
00:10:08,390 --> 00:10:09,390
maybe she wanted us

271
00:10:09,390 --> 00:10:11,550
to take care of each other.

272
00:10:14,150 --> 00:10:15,390
I mean,

273
00:10:15,550 --> 00:10:16,480
you should find

274
00:10:16,480 --> 00:10:17,480
a more respectable job.

275
00:10:17,480 --> 00:10:19,080
I'm only looking out for you.

276
00:10:20,120 --> 00:10:21,720
There's a flaw in your logic.

277
00:10:21,790 --> 00:10:23,440
What's wrong with my job?

278
00:10:23,790 --> 00:10:25,270
Everyone dies someday.

279
00:10:25,440 --> 00:10:27,440
And then they need a box to go in.

280
00:10:28,360 --> 00:10:28,870
Let me tell you,

281
00:10:28,870 --> 00:10:30,530
you'd better be nice to me now.

282
00:10:30,630 --> 00:10:32,430
When your time comes,

283
00:10:32,430 --> 00:10:33,440
I might be kind enough

284
00:10:33,440 --> 00:10:34,670
to find you a nice spot.

285
00:10:34,670 --> 00:10:35,600
Liu Zhengguang!

286
00:10:36,480 --> 00:10:37,960
Don't joke about that.

287
00:10:38,270 --> 00:10:40,530
Doctors can't stand hearing that stuff.

288
00:10:41,750 --> 00:10:43,280
What's wrong with doctors?

289
00:10:43,600 --> 00:10:44,480
I bet you don't even make

290
00:10:44,480 --> 00:10:45,790
as much as Ms. Aichen.

291
00:10:46,120 --> 00:10:47,720
We're nothing alike.

292
00:10:47,750 --> 00:10:49,610
Making money off dying patients?

293
00:10:49,960 --> 00:10:51,760
No amount of money is worth that.

294
00:10:58,910 --> 00:10:59,840
Liu Zhengliang.

295
00:11:01,870 --> 00:11:02,750
Bro.

296
00:11:04,720 --> 00:11:05,550
What's up?

297
00:11:06,840 --> 00:11:08,270
Can we talk like normal people?

298
00:11:08,270 --> 00:11:09,030
Fine.

299
00:11:10,000 --> 00:11:11,360
I do want to change jobs,

300
00:11:11,720 --> 00:11:13,120
but Aichen's parents

301
00:11:13,120 --> 00:11:14,520
are old friends of Mom's.

302
00:11:14,790 --> 00:11:16,070
Uncle Ai and Aunt Mi.

303
00:11:16,070 --> 00:11:17,270
Do you remember them?

304
00:11:18,720 --> 00:11:20,980
Mom mentioned them. I vaguely remember.

305
00:11:21,200 --> 00:11:22,510
With that connection,

306
00:11:22,720 --> 00:11:24,580
I can't just tell her I'm leaving.

307
00:11:24,600 --> 00:11:26,000
What's so hard about that?

308
00:11:26,000 --> 00:11:27,330
Just tell her straight.

309
00:11:29,960 --> 00:11:31,560
Why don't you tell her for me?

310
00:11:34,080 --> 00:11:35,670
Why should I do that?

311
00:11:37,750 --> 00:11:39,510
Are you scared of her?

312
00:11:40,080 --> 00:11:41,080
Too chicken to go?

313
00:11:48,550 --> 00:11:49,600
Give me the address.

314
00:11:49,600 --> 00:11:56,390
"Dad, tomorrow
you'll ride off to the West.

315
00:11:49,760 --> 00:11:52,250
[Fucheng Funeral Services Street]

316
00:11:52,410 --> 00:11:55,550
[Xiao'an Paper Offerings Shop]

317
00:11:56,790 --> 00:12:01,870
Your child bows before you.

318
00:12:02,600 --> 00:12:06,150
Calling out, 'Dad!'

319
00:12:06,240 --> 00:12:09,840
Crying, 'Oh, Dad!'

320
00:12:10,120 --> 00:12:20,390
Dad, take it slow on your way tomorrow!"

321
00:12:27,240 --> 00:12:28,000
Hey, girl,

322
00:12:28,670 --> 00:12:30,530
getting the hang of the business?

323
00:12:31,600 --> 00:12:33,200
You know, in our line of work,

324
00:12:33,200 --> 00:12:35,000
nothing should be taboo.

325
00:12:36,790 --> 00:12:39,550
But next time you cry,

326
00:12:39,550 --> 00:12:41,080
don't cry for your dad.

327
00:12:42,120 --> 00:12:43,050
Cry for your mom.

328
00:12:43,120 --> 00:12:44,360
No, I mean...

329
00:12:45,630 --> 00:12:46,830
Cry for your grandpa.

330
00:12:49,030 --> 00:12:50,670
Sorry about that, Third Brother.

331
00:12:50,670 --> 00:12:52,550
I'll change it right away.

332
00:13:24,390 --> 00:13:26,480
One-three-one-four.

333
00:13:26,480 --> 00:13:28,140
Right, one-three-one-four.

334
00:13:28,910 --> 00:13:30,120
One-three-one-four.

335
00:13:30,120 --> 00:13:31,050
That works, too.

336
00:13:32,360 --> 00:13:33,620
One-three-one-four.

337
00:13:34,870 --> 00:13:36,130
One-three-one-four.

338
00:13:39,910 --> 00:13:41,240
Something's not right.

339
00:13:41,240 --> 00:13:42,120
What's wrong?

340
00:13:44,150 --> 00:13:46,030
I entered the Morse code for 1314,

341
00:13:46,240 --> 00:13:48,030
but the message didn't get through.

342
00:13:48,030 --> 00:13:48,550
This...

343
00:13:54,960 --> 00:13:56,480
No wonder they leave here

344
00:13:56,480 --> 00:13:57,360
in tears.

345
00:13:57,840 --> 00:13:59,150
Did the mission fail?

346
00:14:01,320 --> 00:14:02,550
No, you... you're...

347
00:14:02,550 --> 00:14:03,360
Chief,

348
00:14:03,440 --> 00:14:04,770
don't you recognize me?

349
00:14:06,360 --> 00:14:07,360
Comrade Xiaobo sent me

350
00:14:07,360 --> 00:14:08,550
to be your adjutant.

351
00:14:08,600 --> 00:14:09,910
Who's Xiaobo?

352
00:14:10,240 --> 00:14:11,440
Don't ask questions you shouldn't.

353
00:14:11,440 --> 00:14:12,440
That's protocol.

354
00:14:13,000 --> 00:14:14,000
He's my superior.

355
00:14:16,440 --> 00:14:17,640
Did the mission fail?

356
00:14:18,240 --> 00:14:18,840
Comrade,

357
00:14:19,440 --> 00:14:20,970
the mission hasn't failed.

358
00:14:21,750 --> 00:14:23,150
The organization wants you

359
00:14:23,150 --> 00:14:25,120
to take care of yourself

360
00:14:25,600 --> 00:14:27,200
and await your next mission.

361
00:14:28,240 --> 00:14:29,270
The organization hasn't forgotten me?

362
00:14:29,270 --> 00:14:30,240
Of course not.

363
00:14:30,750 --> 00:14:32,180
I promise I'll complete the mission.

364
00:14:32,180 --> 00:14:36,230
[1314 Funeral Services]

365
00:14:32,240 --> 00:14:33,440
Rest assured, Chief.

366
00:14:34,390 --> 00:14:35,440
You all take care.

367
00:14:35,440 --> 00:14:36,390
Stay alert.

368
00:14:36,840 --> 00:14:37,440
All right.

369
00:14:37,790 --> 00:14:38,510
Take care.

370
00:14:39,750 --> 00:14:40,440
Keep a low profile.

371
00:14:40,440 --> 00:14:41,240
Don't worry.

372
00:14:43,080 --> 00:14:44,340
Don't worry, Comrade.

373
00:14:52,200 --> 00:14:53,360
Where have you been?

374
00:14:53,360 --> 00:14:55,160
You wouldn't answer your phone.

375
00:14:56,000 --> 00:14:57,390
This is for the secret rendezvous.

376
00:14:57,390 --> 00:14:58,510
What's this thing?

377
00:14:59,750 --> 00:15:00,320
Sis...

378
00:15:00,750 --> 00:15:01,510
He's a lunatic.

379
00:15:01,510 --> 00:15:03,000
Can't you give me a break?

380
00:15:03,480 --> 00:15:04,790
- You even played along.
- Look at you,

381
00:15:04,790 --> 00:15:06,390
you're only getting fatter and dumber.

382
00:15:06,390 --> 00:15:07,150
Didn't you notice

383
00:15:07,150 --> 00:15:08,320
how neat and tidy he was,

384
00:15:08,320 --> 00:15:09,600
how clean he looked?

385
00:15:09,600 --> 00:15:10,390
So what does that prove?

386
00:15:10,390 --> 00:15:11,600
That he just got sick.

387
00:15:12,120 --> 00:15:13,600
It proves someone's looking after him,

388
00:15:13,600 --> 00:15:14,360
you know?

389
00:15:14,550 --> 00:15:15,240
People like him

390
00:15:15,240 --> 00:15:16,840
won't hurt anyone.

391
00:15:17,000 --> 00:15:17,960
I don't buy it.

392
00:15:18,240 --> 00:15:19,240
If someone's looking after him,

393
00:15:19,240 --> 00:15:21,040
why let him wander around alone?

394
00:15:21,360 --> 00:15:22,840
What's all that noise?

395
00:15:32,510 --> 00:15:33,840
Is that a marching band?

396
00:15:34,150 --> 00:15:35,510
Must be that new-style funeral crew

397
00:15:35,510 --> 00:15:36,670
that just popped up.

398
00:15:37,120 --> 00:15:39,120
They're ridiculously over the top.

399
00:15:39,200 --> 00:15:40,120
They even offer

400
00:15:40,120 --> 00:15:41,840
spa treatments for the dead.

401
00:15:42,150 --> 00:15:43,360
New-style?

402
00:15:44,320 --> 00:15:45,480
Who's behind it?

403
00:15:45,510 --> 00:15:46,670
A local.

404
00:15:46,840 --> 00:15:48,550
I hear they studied abroad.

405
00:15:46,920 --> 00:15:48,940
[Daxi Fried Snacks]

406
00:15:49,120 --> 00:15:50,390
They don't play fair.

407
00:15:50,630 --> 00:15:51,910
They've got people in every hospital

408
00:15:51,910 --> 00:15:53,030
stealing our business.

409
00:15:53,030 --> 00:15:54,000
How dare they!

410
00:16:05,510 --> 00:16:06,840
What are you doing here?

411
00:16:09,080 --> 00:16:10,210
Let's talk outside.

412
00:16:14,240 --> 00:16:15,170
What's going on?

413
00:16:16,320 --> 00:16:18,520
Has Zhengguang's condition worsened?

414
00:16:18,600 --> 00:16:19,390
No.

415
00:16:20,120 --> 00:16:21,520
I just need to talk to you.

416
00:16:22,150 --> 00:16:23,810
What do you want to talk about?

417
00:16:27,120 --> 00:16:28,480
They're dating?

418
00:16:29,390 --> 00:16:30,600
I didn't know, Dad.

419
00:16:30,790 --> 00:16:32,390
What a brave soul.

420
00:16:33,630 --> 00:16:36,430
That brave soul looks
like Zhengguang's brother.

421
00:16:37,510 --> 00:16:38,000
Hello?

422
00:16:38,000 --> 00:16:38,960
Where are you?

423
00:16:40,240 --> 00:16:41,790
Why hasn't anyone come to pick me up?

424
00:16:41,790 --> 00:16:43,080
Isn't it next month?

425
00:16:43,480 --> 00:16:44,630
I want to talk to you

426
00:16:44,630 --> 00:16:45,870
about Liu Zhengguang's future

427
00:16:45,870 --> 00:16:47,400
and his big life decisions.

428
00:16:48,270 --> 00:16:49,510
Well...

429
00:16:50,120 --> 00:16:50,870
Not a chance.

430
00:16:51,440 --> 00:16:53,370
I'm not interested in younger men.

431
00:16:55,000 --> 00:16:55,670
No.

432
00:16:55,670 --> 00:16:56,360
Aichen,

433
00:16:56,360 --> 00:16:57,200
your mom's here.

434
00:16:57,200 --> 00:16:58,000
Go get her.

435
00:16:59,270 --> 00:17:00,120
I'm getting Mom!

436
00:17:00,120 --> 00:17:01,320
Hurry! Move!

437
00:17:04,270 --> 00:17:05,510
Sis, wait for me!

438
00:17:11,740 --> 00:17:15,450
[Prison]

439
00:17:27,750 --> 00:17:28,720
Mom!

440
00:17:29,350 --> 00:17:30,830
I've missed you so much!

441
00:17:33,960 --> 00:17:35,000
Your poor little face is freezing.

442
00:17:35,000 --> 00:17:36,200
Here, put this on.

443
00:17:36,790 --> 00:17:37,350
Let's go home.

444
00:17:37,350 --> 00:17:37,810
Come on.

445
00:17:38,110 --> 00:17:39,110
We're going home.

446
00:17:44,800 --> 00:17:49,660
[1314 Funeral Services]

447
00:17:52,480 --> 00:17:53,610
Come sit in the back.

448
00:18:15,920 --> 00:18:17,400
Did you deliberately get the time wrong

449
00:18:17,400 --> 00:18:18,590
because you didn't want to pick me up?

450
00:18:18,590 --> 00:18:19,520
Absolutely not.

451
00:18:21,030 --> 00:18:21,750
Sit closer.

452
00:18:23,270 --> 00:18:25,110
Amy, I'm sorry.

453
00:18:25,310 --> 00:18:26,440
What did you call me?

454
00:18:26,480 --> 00:18:27,960
Who are you talking to?

455
00:18:28,240 --> 00:18:30,200
I gave your mom a new name:

456
00:18:30,720 --> 00:18:34,310
Ai San Loves Mi Si the Most.

457
00:18:35,110 --> 00:18:35,830
That's too long,

458
00:18:35,830 --> 00:18:38,480
so I shortened it to Amy.

459
00:18:38,060 --> 00:18:40,940
[1314 Funeral Services]

460
00:18:39,310 --> 00:18:39,920
Come here.

461
00:18:40,920 --> 00:18:42,680
Amy, I'm sorry.

462
00:18:46,960 --> 00:18:49,680
Long live freedom!

463
00:18:49,880 --> 00:18:51,240
"We're different.

464
00:18:51,240 --> 00:18:53,440
Different, different..."

465
00:18:55,310 --> 00:18:57,140
[Fucheng Huaide Funeral Center]

466
00:18:57,180 --> 00:19:01,400
[1314 Funeral Services]

467
00:18:57,720 --> 00:18:58,920
I'll go open the door.

468
00:18:59,790 --> 00:19:01,880
Street music and square dancing.

469
00:19:02,110 --> 00:19:04,000
They're all Northeastern songs.

470
00:19:05,200 --> 00:19:06,510
Why are you still here?

471
00:19:06,750 --> 00:19:07,790
I was waiting for you,

472
00:19:07,530 --> 00:19:10,910
[Complete Funeral Services]

473
00:19:08,160 --> 00:19:10,020
who ran off before I could finish.

474
00:19:10,350 --> 00:19:11,440
You're unbelievable.

475
00:19:11,440 --> 00:19:13,510
It's a two-hour round trip for us.

476
00:19:13,510 --> 00:19:14,240
Come on.

477
00:19:14,240 --> 00:19:15,350
Let's talk inside.

478
00:19:15,590 --> 00:19:16,640
No, let's talk here.

479
00:19:16,640 --> 00:19:17,750
I'll be quick.

480
00:19:18,160 --> 00:19:19,020
The thing is...

481
00:19:19,830 --> 00:19:20,880
Who's this young man?

482
00:19:20,880 --> 00:19:22,210
Zhengguang's brother.

483
00:19:26,960 --> 00:19:29,020
The doctor who came up from the South.

484
00:19:29,680 --> 00:19:31,880
He's better-looking than Zhengguang.

485
00:19:33,960 --> 00:19:35,240
Let's talk inside.

486
00:19:35,310 --> 00:19:35,880
No need.

487
00:19:38,110 --> 00:19:40,110
I'll get you a chair, then.

488
00:19:40,110 --> 00:19:40,590
No need.

489
00:19:44,160 --> 00:19:46,000
I'll get you something to drink.

490
00:19:46,000 --> 00:19:46,680
No need.

491
00:19:52,590 --> 00:19:53,920
Take your time talking.

492
00:19:54,310 --> 00:19:55,590
I'll get straight to the point.

493
00:19:55,590 --> 00:19:56,550
I'm here on Liu Zhengguang's behalf

494
00:19:56,550 --> 00:19:57,400
to let you know

495
00:19:57,400 --> 00:19:58,200
that once he's discharged,

496
00:19:58,200 --> 00:19:59,310
he won't be working for you anymore.

497
00:19:59,310 --> 00:20:00,110
Why not?

498
00:20:01,880 --> 00:20:03,480
He wants a different job.

499
00:20:04,750 --> 00:20:05,750
What kind of job?

500
00:20:06,110 --> 00:20:07,070
He hasn't decided yet,

501
00:20:07,070 --> 00:20:08,870
but this one isn't right for him.

502
00:20:09,350 --> 00:20:10,960
Is that what you think,

503
00:20:10,960 --> 00:20:12,110
or does he think so?

504
00:20:13,680 --> 00:20:15,590
He wants a change.

505
00:20:15,790 --> 00:20:16,400
Of course,

506
00:20:16,400 --> 00:20:17,440
I agree with him too.

507
00:20:17,440 --> 00:20:18,240
Get lost!

508
00:20:18,880 --> 00:20:20,310
Putting on an act, huh?

509
00:20:20,720 --> 00:20:21,160
Just now,

510
00:20:21,160 --> 00:20:22,720
you were too cool to talk, huh?

511
00:20:22,720 --> 00:20:24,640
That's my dad, got it?

512
00:20:25,310 --> 00:20:26,960
Wasn't he welcoming enough?

513
00:20:28,270 --> 00:20:29,310
You're something else.

514
00:20:29,310 --> 00:20:31,170
You wouldn't even give him a look.

515
00:20:31,680 --> 00:20:33,010
Who do you think you are?

516
00:20:33,200 --> 00:20:34,790
Standing there,

517
00:20:34,790 --> 00:20:35,590
like a telephone pole

518
00:20:35,590 --> 00:20:36,880
with extra ears.

519
00:20:37,200 --> 00:20:38,750
You shouldn't be called Zhengliang.

520
00:20:38,750 --> 00:20:40,150
You're "Pole with Ears."

521
00:20:40,720 --> 00:20:42,050
What are you staring at?

522
00:20:42,790 --> 00:20:43,960
You look down on funeral workers,

523
00:20:43,960 --> 00:20:44,560
don't you?

524
00:20:45,440 --> 00:20:47,110
Sis!

525
00:20:47,440 --> 00:20:47,880
There's a man at First Hospital

526
00:20:47,880 --> 00:20:48,590
who's on his last legs.

527
00:20:48,590 --> 00:20:49,320
Are we going?

528
00:20:52,920 --> 00:20:54,110
I-I don't care!

529
00:20:54,510 --> 00:20:56,400
I don't care what line of work you're in.

530
00:20:56,400 --> 00:20:56,960
But my brother

531
00:20:56,960 --> 00:20:58,200
won't be working for you anymore.

532
00:20:58,200 --> 00:20:59,070
I hope you understand.

533
00:20:59,070 --> 00:21:00,130
Understand my ass!

534
00:21:00,480 --> 00:21:01,940
Did you come to make a wish?

535
00:21:03,310 --> 00:21:05,480
Such foul language. No class at all.

536
00:21:07,110 --> 00:21:08,160
Let me show you

537
00:21:08,270 --> 00:21:10,510
a failure of character education.

538
00:21:11,900 --> 00:21:13,110
[Complete Funeral Services]

539
00:21:12,160 --> 00:21:13,620
I'm not finished talking!

540
00:21:14,310 --> 00:21:15,310
I don't care!

541
00:21:15,680 --> 00:21:17,070
I don't care if you agree or not.

542
00:21:17,070 --> 00:21:18,400
Once Liu Zhengguang is discharged,

543
00:21:18,400 --> 00:21:19,440
he's done working here.

544
00:21:19,440 --> 00:21:20,270
Got it?

545
00:21:21,270 --> 00:21:21,920
Wait.

546
00:21:24,030 --> 00:21:25,360
What are you getting at?

547
00:21:27,350 --> 00:21:28,960
We live under the rule of law,

548
00:21:28,960 --> 00:21:30,070
in broad daylight.

549
00:21:30,310 --> 00:21:31,640
Who are you trying to scare?

550
00:21:31,640 --> 00:21:33,440
Come on, hit me here.

551
00:21:33,440 --> 00:21:34,480
Go ahead, try it.

552
00:21:34,480 --> 00:21:35,640
Fine, I'll do it!

553
00:21:35,640 --> 00:21:36,350
So what?

554
00:21:37,270 --> 00:21:37,750
Hey!

555
00:21:37,750 --> 00:21:38,310
Shouting at me, huh?

556
00:21:38,310 --> 00:21:39,480
Wait!

557
00:21:39,480 --> 00:21:40,480
Hold on!

558
00:21:40,480 --> 00:21:41,810
I-I'll call the police!

559
00:21:43,550 --> 00:21:43,920
I'm telling you,

560
00:21:43,920 --> 00:21:45,650
I'll call the police right now!

561
00:21:46,720 --> 00:21:48,380
You wanna pick a fight with me?

562
00:21:56,480 --> 00:21:57,590
Just you wait!

563
00:21:57,790 --> 00:21:59,190
I'll beat you senseless!

564
00:22:01,450 --> 00:22:04,040
[Xiaoximen Hospital]
[Starry Night]

565
00:22:10,810 --> 00:22:11,920
[Surgical Inpatient Department]

566
00:22:12,960 --> 00:22:14,160
What's wrong, bro?

567
00:22:14,350 --> 00:22:15,550
Did you get beaten up?

568
00:22:15,960 --> 00:22:17,270
Just your bad luck.

569
00:22:17,720 --> 00:22:19,680
I knew you'd get your ass kicked.

570
00:22:23,350 --> 00:22:24,350
Mom said

571
00:22:24,350 --> 00:22:25,810
you have to take care of me.

572
00:22:33,920 --> 00:22:35,050
Some doctor you are.

573
00:22:35,430 --> 00:22:38,070
[ICU is on Floor 2]

574
00:22:58,550 --> 00:22:59,680
Who are you here to see?

575
00:22:59,680 --> 00:23:01,680
I'm here to report to Director Tong.

576
00:23:03,110 --> 00:23:04,270
He's not here right now.

577
00:23:04,270 --> 00:23:05,550
You can tell me what you need.

578
00:23:05,550 --> 00:23:06,210
That works.

579
00:23:06,880 --> 00:23:07,830
And you are?

580
00:23:09,400 --> 00:23:10,720
I'm Song Jian.

581
00:23:10,720 --> 00:23:11,960
Just call me Dr. Song.

582
00:23:14,030 --> 00:23:14,880
Dr. Song.

583
00:23:16,680 --> 00:23:17,590
How many years?

584
00:23:19,000 --> 00:23:20,200
How'd you end up here?

585
00:23:20,440 --> 00:23:21,640
You mean my contract?

586
00:23:23,200 --> 00:23:24,590
The president tricked me

587
00:23:24,590 --> 00:23:26,120
into signing a 5-year deal.

588
00:23:27,750 --> 00:23:29,240
Now you're talking.

589
00:23:30,030 --> 00:23:32,750
This place is nothing but a scam.

590
00:23:33,270 --> 00:23:34,350
Look at me.

591
00:23:34,750 --> 00:23:36,240
Fifteen years.

592
00:23:36,350 --> 00:23:37,680
Fifteen years?

593
00:23:37,680 --> 00:23:38,550
You bet.

594
00:23:38,550 --> 00:23:39,750
They tricked you too?

595
00:23:41,590 --> 00:23:42,720
-Song Jian.
-So, I'm telling you about this place...

596
00:23:42,720 --> 00:23:43,350
What are you doing here?

597
00:23:43,350 --> 00:23:43,920
Listen to me.

598
00:23:43,920 --> 00:23:45,160
-Where’s your family?
-Go! Go!

599
00:23:45,160 --> 00:23:45,720
Let's go.

600
00:23:45,720 --> 00:23:46,640
What are you doing?

601
00:23:46,640 --> 00:23:47,920
I'm just chatting with my buddy.

602
00:23:47,920 --> 00:23:48,680
How rude.

603
00:23:48,790 --> 00:23:50,960
Come on, have a seat, buddy.

604
00:23:51,400 --> 00:23:52,160
Sorry about that.

605
00:23:52,160 --> 00:23:53,000
This patient was
just released from prison.

606
00:23:53,000 --> 00:23:53,750
He's got some mental issues.

607
00:23:53,750 --> 00:23:54,480
The big hospitals wouldn't take him,

608
00:23:54,480 --> 00:23:55,640
so they sent him here.

609
00:23:55,640 --> 00:23:56,840
What are you here for?

610
00:23:58,480 --> 00:23:59,920
I... I'm here to report to Director Tong.

611
00:23:59,920 --> 00:24:00,960
He's next door.

612
00:24:11,430 --> 00:24:13,500
[Director's Office]

613
00:24:17,240 --> 00:24:17,960
Come in.

614
00:24:18,430 --> 00:24:26,090
[Hot Water: Handle
with Care to Avoid Scalding]

615
00:24:19,400 --> 00:24:21,110
Hello, Director Tong.

616
00:24:21,110 --> 00:24:22,640
I'm here to report for duty.

617
00:24:22,680 --> 00:24:23,340
Have a seat.

618
00:24:23,550 --> 00:24:24,880
Liu Zhengliang, right?

619
00:24:30,350 --> 00:24:31,440
To be honest,

620
00:24:33,030 --> 00:24:34,070
I'm not too keen on you

621
00:24:34,070 --> 00:24:35,330
joining our hospital.

622
00:24:35,480 --> 00:24:37,310
After all, you came back from a big city.

623
00:24:37,310 --> 00:24:39,200
I don't think you'll fit in

624
00:24:39,200 --> 00:24:40,750
with the way things work here.

625
00:24:40,750 --> 00:24:41,590
I think you're

626
00:24:41,590 --> 00:24:42,680
absolutely right.

627
00:24:43,440 --> 00:24:44,440
Right about what?

628
00:24:46,160 --> 00:24:48,000
I owe you an apology

629
00:24:49,070 --> 00:24:50,400
for what I said earlier.

630
00:24:50,750 --> 00:24:51,350
The reason

631
00:24:51,350 --> 00:24:53,110
I had those thoughts before

632
00:24:54,160 --> 00:24:55,720
was that I had a narrow outlook.

633
00:24:55,720 --> 00:24:57,520
But the president is different.

634
00:24:58,030 --> 00:24:59,640
He's a man of vision.

635
00:25:00,640 --> 00:25:01,440
He said,

636
00:25:02,830 --> 00:25:05,790
"A doctor is like a pair of chopsticks.
Long or short, both come in handy.

637
00:25:05,790 --> 00:25:07,990
Treating patients is like fixing cars.

638
00:25:08,000 --> 00:25:09,070
No matter the size of the wrench,

639
00:25:09,070 --> 00:25:11,270
if it can turn a screw, it's a good tool."

640
00:25:11,400 --> 00:25:13,000
Now that's real wisdom.

641
00:25:14,350 --> 00:25:16,070
It really opens your eyes.

642
00:25:16,480 --> 00:25:19,010
I don't think that's
quite appropriate here.

643
00:25:20,350 --> 00:25:21,240
When the president speaks,

644
00:25:21,240 --> 00:25:22,590
you just listen.

645
00:25:24,640 --> 00:25:26,240
And listening isn't enough.

646
00:25:27,160 --> 00:25:28,560
You have to think it over.

647
00:25:28,590 --> 00:25:29,520
Savor his words.

648
00:25:33,640 --> 00:25:35,040
You've got a lot to learn.

649
00:25:56,720 --> 00:25:57,320
By the way,

650
00:25:59,830 --> 00:26:00,880
our Neurosurgical Department

651
00:26:00,880 --> 00:26:02,640
hardly has any patients.

652
00:26:03,640 --> 00:26:06,040
We almost have more doctors than patients.

653
00:26:06,480 --> 00:26:08,240
As for the rules at Xiaoximen,

654
00:26:08,240 --> 00:26:10,030
emergency surgery duty rotates

655
00:26:10,030 --> 00:26:12,790
among the surgical departments.

656
00:26:12,880 --> 00:26:14,480
This quarter, it's our turn.

657
00:26:14,680 --> 00:26:15,510
Che Mingming,

658
00:26:15,640 --> 00:26:16,920
the doctor

659
00:26:16,920 --> 00:26:18,590
who assisted you that day,

660
00:26:18,590 --> 00:26:19,960
has already reported for duty.

661
00:26:19,960 --> 00:26:21,760
Go straight to the ER and see her.

662
00:26:23,680 --> 00:26:24,540
One more thing.

663
00:26:24,880 --> 00:26:26,440
You still have to keep up with

664
00:26:26,440 --> 00:26:28,440
your department's regular duties.

665
00:26:28,720 --> 00:26:29,480
Right now, you only have

666
00:26:29,480 --> 00:26:30,960
your brother as a patient,

667
00:26:31,070 --> 00:26:32,670
so you've got it pretty easy.

668
00:26:50,380 --> 00:26:52,770
[For comedic effect only.
Please follow your doctor's instructions]
[Metronidazole Tablets]

669
00:26:50,480 --> 00:26:51,550
Don't get the wrong idea.

670
00:26:51,550 --> 00:26:52,790
This is metronidazole.

671
00:26:52,790 --> 00:26:59,190
[For comedic effect only.
Please follow your doctor's instructions]

672
00:26:55,400 --> 00:26:57,000
The president's sister-in-law told me

673
00:26:57,000 --> 00:26:58,270
that if you crush it up

674
00:26:58,270 --> 00:27:00,200
and sniff it, it'll cure rhinitis.

675
00:27:04,160 --> 00:27:05,680
I go through so much tissue
because of my rhinitis.

676
00:27:05,680 --> 00:27:06,590
I spend several bucks a day

677
00:27:06,590 --> 00:27:07,520
just on tissues.

678
00:27:08,350 --> 00:27:10,000
So it was metronidazole all along.

679
00:27:10,000 --> 00:27:10,720
Scared you, huh?

680
00:27:10,720 --> 00:27:11,920
I hate that stuff too.

681
00:27:14,200 --> 00:27:15,240
All right, Director.

682
00:27:15,240 --> 00:27:16,590
I'll head to the ER now.

683
00:27:16,920 --> 00:27:17,480
Go ahead.

684
00:27:22,400 --> 00:27:23,400
Wait a minute.

685
00:27:23,920 --> 00:27:25,270
Metronidazole for rhinitis?

686
00:27:25,270 --> 00:27:26,880
And you're applying it topically?

687
00:27:26,880 --> 00:27:28,830
Is there any scientific basis for that?

688
00:27:28,830 --> 00:27:30,000
Which hospital

689
00:27:30,000 --> 00:27:30,880
does the president's sister-in-law

690
00:27:30,880 --> 00:27:32,000
work at as an ENT specialist?

691
00:27:32,000 --> 00:27:33,030
What specialist?

692
00:27:33,550 --> 00:27:34,550
The president's sister-in-law

693
00:27:34,550 --> 00:27:36,270
is an accountant
at Qiaoxi Elementary School.

694
00:27:36,270 --> 00:27:36,750
You...

695
00:27:37,400 --> 00:27:39,030
You're the director
of Neurosurgical Department,

696
00:27:39,030 --> 00:27:40,480
and you're treating yourself
with some folk remedy

697
00:27:40,480 --> 00:27:42,210
recommended by an accountant?

698
00:27:44,110 --> 00:27:45,200
The president's sister-in-law

699
00:27:45,200 --> 00:27:46,830
is no ordinary person.

700
00:27:48,960 --> 00:27:49,790
You might think

701
00:27:49,790 --> 00:27:51,250
I'm just sucking up to him,

702
00:27:51,550 --> 00:27:52,610
but I'm really not.

703
00:27:56,750 --> 00:27:58,920
You'll understand in time.

704
00:28:01,070 --> 00:28:02,270
Do you have rhinitis?

705
00:28:04,850 --> 00:28:08,010
[Accessible Route]

706
00:28:17,910 --> 00:28:22,340
[Hospital Admission Registration]

707
00:28:26,720 --> 00:28:27,510
Stop!

708
00:28:27,750 --> 00:28:31,270
-Bro, run! Why are you chasing me?
-Song Jian! Stop!

709
00:28:31,440 --> 00:28:32,430
Song Jian, don't run!

710
00:28:32,430 --> 00:28:33,440
How rude.

711
00:28:34,350 --> 00:28:34,790
You...

712
00:28:36,830 --> 00:28:37,590
Waiter!

713
00:28:37,590 --> 00:28:39,000
Get me a pair of slippers.

714
00:28:39,160 --> 00:28:41,550
And open another bottle
of 30-year-old Moutai.

715
00:28:41,550 --> 00:28:42,270
What's going on?

716
00:28:42,270 --> 00:28:44,470
He's messed up his brain from drinking.

717
00:29:14,510 --> 00:29:15,420
[Emergency Department]

718
00:29:35,320 --> 00:29:39,480
[Fucheng Bank]

719
00:29:53,110 --> 00:29:54,110
-The ER...
-Doctor.

720
00:29:54,110 --> 00:29:54,830
Doctor.

721
00:29:54,130 --> 00:29:54,920
[Interpreting Treatise on the Spleen and
Stomach Through Five Circuits and Six Qi]

722
00:29:55,070 --> 00:29:56,130
Take a look at this.

723
00:29:56,240 --> 00:29:57,750
There's something stuck in here.

724
00:29:57,750 --> 00:29:58,680
It hurts so much.

725
00:29:59,880 --> 00:30:01,160
If something's stuck between your teeth,

726
00:30:01,160 --> 00:30:02,350
just pick it out yourself.

727
00:30:02,350 --> 00:30:04,240
Doctor, how can you say that?

728
00:30:04,750 --> 00:30:06,110
If I could get it out myself at home,

729
00:30:06,110 --> 00:30:07,830
why would I come to a doctor?

730
00:30:07,960 --> 00:30:08,920
Am I right?

731
00:30:09,240 --> 00:30:10,270
Open your mouth.

732
00:30:12,680 --> 00:30:13,740
Come on, open wide.

733
00:30:14,310 --> 00:30:15,350
Come on, open up.

734
00:30:16,590 --> 00:30:17,400
Which tooth?

735
00:30:17,510 --> 00:30:18,400
This one at the bottom. This one.

736
00:30:18,400 --> 00:30:19,460
This one down here.

737
00:30:19,480 --> 00:30:20,240
Where? This side?

738
00:30:20,240 --> 00:30:20,880
This side.

739
00:30:22,680 --> 00:30:23,750
What's all the yelling for?

740
00:30:23,750 --> 00:30:24,350
Open your mouth.

741
00:30:24,350 --> 00:30:25,480
Easy, doctor! Easy!

742
00:30:26,350 --> 00:30:27,440
It's inflamed
from whatever's stuck in there.

743
00:30:27,440 --> 00:30:28,110
A little.

744
00:30:28,680 --> 00:30:29,920
What kind of bone were you chewing on?

745
00:30:29,920 --> 00:30:30,720
Chicken bone.

746
00:30:30,920 --> 00:30:31,720
Chicken bone?

747
00:30:44,260 --> 00:30:51,850
[Doctor's Office]

748
00:30:45,310 --> 00:30:46,110
Come on.

749
00:30:46,480 --> 00:30:48,070
Are you really that desperate for money?

750
00:30:48,070 --> 00:30:49,790
Why go back to your old line of work?

751
00:30:49,790 --> 00:30:50,960
So what if I go back
to my old line of work?

752
00:30:50,960 --> 00:30:52,350
How does that affect you?

753
00:30:52,350 --> 00:30:53,550
What business is it of yours?

754
00:30:53,550 --> 00:30:55,000
I'm free to do what I want.

755
00:30:55,070 --> 00:30:56,240
Aren't you afraid people will find out

756
00:30:56,240 --> 00:30:57,270
what you used to do?

757
00:30:57,270 --> 00:30:58,720
So what if I used to do that?

758
00:30:58,720 --> 00:30:59,750
You're so high and mighty.

759
00:30:59,750 --> 00:31:00,550
Fine, fine, fine.

760
00:31:00,550 --> 00:31:01,790
You're unbelievably shameless.

761
00:31:01,550 --> 00:31:02,760
[No Unauthorized Entry
into Doctors' Lounge]

762
00:31:01,790 --> 00:31:02,720
I'm telling you.

763
00:31:20,480 --> 00:31:21,270
Hello.

764
00:31:21,510 --> 00:31:22,640
I'm...

765
00:31:24,240 --> 00:31:25,440
I know you.

766
00:31:25,750 --> 00:31:27,640
Liu Zhengliang, right?

767
00:31:28,480 --> 00:31:30,070
I heard this morning you were coming.

768
00:31:30,070 --> 00:31:31,000
Nice to meet you.

769
00:31:31,270 --> 00:31:32,150
I'm Zhang Hao.

770
00:31:32,350 --> 00:31:34,720
Call me Hao or Bro,
whatever you like.

771
00:31:37,270 --> 00:31:38,000
Well...

772
00:31:38,000 --> 00:31:39,310
Come on, come inside.

773
00:31:39,310 --> 00:31:41,440
That break room is shared by everyone.

774
00:31:41,720 --> 00:31:43,960
If anyone needs a bed, ladies first.

775
00:31:44,750 --> 00:31:46,400
Take a look and choose
whichever locker you like.

776
00:31:46,400 --> 00:31:47,260
Help yourself.

777
00:31:58,550 --> 00:31:59,510
Sorry, sorry.

778
00:31:59,510 --> 00:32:01,170
He's new here. He didn't know.

779
00:32:09,830 --> 00:32:11,160
Look at your luck.

780
00:32:11,550 --> 00:32:12,960
I had this spot divined especially.

781
00:32:12,960 --> 00:32:13,830
This is the wealth spot.

782
00:32:13,830 --> 00:32:14,720
Dr. Zhang!

783
00:32:15,000 --> 00:32:16,270
Dr. Zhang!

784
00:32:17,070 --> 00:32:17,830
It's not even noon,

785
00:32:17,830 --> 00:32:20,030
and you've already got drunk patients?

786
00:32:20,350 --> 00:32:21,440
They're two old guys

787
00:32:21,440 --> 00:32:22,790
who came in on a group deal
early this morning.

788
00:32:22,790 --> 00:32:23,920
One was over there belting out songs,

789
00:32:23,920 --> 00:32:24,790
and the other changed the track,

790
00:32:24,790 --> 00:32:25,480
so they got into a fight.

791
00:32:25,480 --> 00:32:26,350
All right, got it.

792
00:32:26,350 --> 00:32:27,110
You got it?

793
00:32:27,110 --> 00:32:27,550
Okay.

794
00:32:27,550 --> 00:32:29,830
Dr. Che, a trauma case!

795
00:32:29,830 --> 00:32:31,030
Patch the patient up.

796
00:32:31,440 --> 00:32:33,000
Where does that door lead?

797
00:32:33,720 --> 00:32:34,750
The fast track,

798
00:32:34,750 --> 00:32:36,030
straight to the karaoke lounge.

799
00:32:36,030 --> 00:32:37,560
I'll show you to the office.

800
00:32:38,050 --> 00:32:38,890
[Doctor's Office]

801
00:32:55,400 --> 00:32:56,350
Sorry about that.

802
00:32:56,350 --> 00:32:57,830
I forgot you were behind me.

803
00:32:57,830 --> 00:32:59,830
How did you manage to open this door?

804
00:33:00,400 --> 00:33:02,070
It's been broken for two years.

805
00:33:02,070 --> 00:33:03,590
You have to find the right trick.

806
00:33:03,590 --> 00:33:04,880
Lift it up a little.

807
00:33:04,880 --> 00:33:06,070
Don't lift it too high.

808
00:33:06,070 --> 00:33:07,730
You have to get the feel for it.

809
00:33:08,000 --> 00:33:08,310
Then turn it, and it opens.

810
00:33:08,310 --> 00:33:09,160
Give it a try.

811
00:33:09,640 --> 00:33:10,480
Go on, try it.

812
00:33:17,270 --> 00:33:17,720
Fine.

813
00:33:19,110 --> 00:33:20,830
Why don't you fix the door?

814
00:33:20,830 --> 00:33:21,030
What's the point?

815
00:33:21,030 --> 00:33:22,000
Oh my god.

816
00:33:22,000 --> 00:33:22,440
What's the point?

817
00:33:22,440 --> 00:33:24,000
Everyone likes it this way.

818
00:33:24,110 --> 00:33:25,200
We don't have to lock the door anymore.

819
00:33:25,200 --> 00:33:26,160
Outsiders can't open it,

820
00:33:26,160 --> 00:33:28,200
but we can with a simple twist.

821
00:33:28,270 --> 00:33:30,030
It's even better than a fingerprint lock.

822
00:33:30,030 --> 00:33:30,680
Some departments

823
00:33:30,680 --> 00:33:32,310
have actually tried to
make their doors work like this.

824
00:33:32,310 --> 00:33:33,200
They studied it for ages

825
00:33:33,200 --> 00:33:34,830
and still couldn't figure out
how it works.

826
00:33:34,830 --> 00:33:35,920
Come in, please.

827
00:33:37,640 --> 00:33:39,500
You can try figuring it out later.

828
00:33:40,310 --> 00:33:41,400
This is the shift handover room.

829
00:33:41,400 --> 00:33:43,530
It's also the office for the four of us.

830
00:33:44,920 --> 00:33:45,830
Which four?

831
00:33:46,000 --> 00:33:47,660
One's in emergency medicine.

832
00:33:47,920 --> 00:33:49,640
I'm from cardiothoracic surgery.

833
00:33:49,640 --> 00:33:51,510
The three of us rotate through surgery,

834
00:33:51,510 --> 00:33:53,070
along with you and Dr. Che.

835
00:33:53,960 --> 00:33:55,110
Don't you have dedicated

836
00:33:55,110 --> 00:33:56,440
emergency surgeons?

837
00:33:57,000 --> 00:33:58,130
This place is small.

838
00:34:02,270 --> 00:34:03,830
This desk is yours.

839
00:34:04,160 --> 00:34:05,830
There's the duty roster over there.

840
00:34:05,830 --> 00:34:07,030
We're not a big hospital

841
00:34:07,030 --> 00:34:07,830
with a day shift,
a night shift, and a day off.

842
00:34:07,830 --> 00:34:08,840
We work day and night shifts in rotation,

843
00:34:08,840 --> 00:34:10,230
with 3 teams taking turns.

844
00:34:10,230 --> 00:34:11,230
No weekends off.

845
00:34:11,280 --> 00:34:12,550
You're on the day shift today,

846
00:34:12,550 --> 00:34:14,590
until 4 this afternoon.

847
00:34:16,960 --> 00:34:17,480
Okay.

848
00:34:17,590 --> 00:34:18,510
You're all set.

849
00:34:34,000 --> 00:34:35,800
Slacking off isn't the problem.

850
00:34:36,110 --> 00:34:38,030
The important thing is to let people know

851
00:34:38,030 --> 00:34:39,230
you're slacking off.

852
00:34:50,400 --> 00:34:52,920
Turn the volume all the way up.

853
00:34:52,960 --> 00:34:54,150
Make sure everyone knows

854
00:34:54,150 --> 00:34:56,480
what you're listening to or watching.

855
00:34:56,480 --> 00:34:57,320
You have to disturb them

856
00:34:57,320 --> 00:34:58,780
to get the desired result.

857
00:35:05,400 --> 00:35:06,630
You watch dramas too?

858
00:35:07,070 --> 00:35:08,670
Which one are you following?

859
00:35:13,840 --> 00:35:14,700
Just whatever.

860
00:35:15,710 --> 00:35:17,230
Pick this thing up.

861
00:35:17,880 --> 00:35:19,280
You need to pick it up and

862
00:35:19,480 --> 00:35:20,630
rub it

863
00:35:20,630 --> 00:35:22,110
to make that grating sound

864
00:35:22,230 --> 00:35:24,360
the kind that makes your teeth ache.

865
00:35:24,510 --> 00:35:26,510
Making noise is the important part.

866
00:35:31,030 --> 00:35:32,550
Smack your lips.

867
00:35:32,550 --> 00:35:33,710
That's right. Spray it out.

868
00:35:33,710 --> 00:35:34,670
The more you spray, the better.

869
00:35:34,670 --> 00:35:35,400
Right in their face.

870
00:35:35,400 --> 00:35:37,200
Got phlegm stuck in your throat?

871
00:35:37,320 --> 00:35:38,780
There's water over there.

872
00:35:44,760 --> 00:35:45,710
You're awake?

873
00:35:46,480 --> 00:35:47,400
Woke up hungry.

874
00:35:47,400 --> 00:35:48,530
Got anything to eat?

875
00:35:54,360 --> 00:35:55,550
Let me introduce him.

876
00:35:55,550 --> 00:35:57,550
This is our new guy, Liu Zhengliang.

877
00:36:00,190 --> 00:36:01,450
Hi, welcome, welcome!

878
00:36:01,960 --> 00:36:03,000
Sorry about that.

879
00:36:04,070 --> 00:36:06,330
I'm Huang Dongsheng.
Just call me Huang.

880
00:36:06,440 --> 00:36:07,400
Nice to meet you.

881
00:36:10,230 --> 00:36:12,920
You just got here
and you're already treating us?

882
00:36:12,920 --> 00:36:14,180
Then I won't hold back.

883
00:36:14,320 --> 00:36:15,580
I'll take one of these.

884
00:36:16,280 --> 00:36:17,680
And another one of these.

885
00:36:20,360 --> 00:36:21,230
Where... where are you...

886
00:36:21,230 --> 00:36:22,290
Where are you from?

887
00:36:22,590 --> 00:36:23,230
Shenzhen.

888
00:36:23,960 --> 00:36:24,880
Shenzhen?

889
00:36:24,880 --> 00:36:26,680
That's a special economic zone!

890
00:36:29,110 --> 00:36:31,510
Even when you sleep,
you need to make some noise.

891
00:36:31,510 --> 00:36:33,440
After you put on the neck pillow...

892
00:36:36,880 --> 00:36:38,680
I'm sleepy. I'm gonna take a nap.

893
00:36:39,480 --> 00:36:42,080
You don't sound sleepy.
That was one loud yawn.

894
00:36:42,480 --> 00:36:43,540
What are you doing?

895
00:36:45,840 --> 00:36:46,770
What do you mean?

896
00:36:47,190 --> 00:36:48,190
Can't I sleep?

897
00:36:48,230 --> 00:36:49,030
No.

898
00:36:57,800 --> 00:36:59,660
Come over here and sleep. Come on.

899
00:37:00,030 --> 00:37:00,880
Come here.

900
00:37:04,400 --> 00:37:05,710
What's with that thing around your neck?

901
00:37:05,710 --> 00:37:07,000
None of this stuff works.

902
00:37:07,000 --> 00:37:07,800
Come here. Listen to me.

903
00:37:07,800 --> 00:37:08,860
Come on, over here.

904
00:37:10,760 --> 00:37:11,550
You...

905
00:37:11,550 --> 00:37:13,150
Come on, sit tight.

906
00:37:13,150 --> 00:37:14,210
Come on, sit tight.

907
00:37:17,280 --> 00:37:18,150
Lie flat.

908
00:37:18,710 --> 00:37:20,110
Doesn't that feel great?

909
00:37:20,110 --> 00:37:21,630
You need to enjoy life. You...

910
00:37:21,630 --> 00:37:22,830
What the heck is this?

911
00:37:29,150 --> 00:37:30,210
Feels good, right?

912
00:37:32,880 --> 00:37:33,840
Close your eyes.

913
00:37:35,400 --> 00:37:36,190
Relax.

914
00:37:38,440 --> 00:37:39,230
Shenzhen.

915
00:37:40,190 --> 00:37:42,790
I think I had a classmate
who lived in Shenzhen.

916
00:38:20,000 --> 00:38:22,320
At that moment,
I could think of only one thing.

917
00:38:22,320 --> 00:38:24,800
A bad environment slowly kills you.

918
00:38:25,280 --> 00:38:26,710
I figured there was a 99% chance

919
00:38:26,710 --> 00:38:28,510
I couldn't survive in this dump.

920
00:38:28,840 --> 00:38:30,440
I left a 1% chance open,

921
00:38:30,880 --> 00:38:32,810
thanks to my instincts as a doctor.

922
00:38:33,960 --> 00:38:36,090
I've always been a meticulous person.

923
00:38:36,980 --> 00:38:41,070
[Emergency Access Route; No Parking]

924
00:38:37,440 --> 00:38:38,640
There's a slope here.

925
00:38:41,630 --> 00:38:42,440
Okay.

926
00:38:43,510 --> 00:38:44,710
There's another one.

927
00:38:46,220 --> 00:38:48,090
[Emergency Vehicle Access; No Parking]

928
00:38:48,580 --> 00:38:52,040
[No Passengers Allowed]

929
00:38:48,800 --> 00:38:50,130
We're here. We're here.

930
00:38:52,960 --> 00:38:54,670
Why'd you bring me here?

931
00:38:54,670 --> 00:38:55,550
To see a doctor.

932
00:38:55,840 --> 00:38:56,590
Well...

933
00:38:56,880 --> 00:38:58,960
I haven't finished my work yet.

934
00:38:58,960 --> 00:39:00,560
Forget about that. Hurry up.

935
00:39:00,760 --> 00:39:02,400
What are you doing?

936
00:39:02,400 --> 00:39:03,480
Listen to me, Mom.

937
00:39:04,030 --> 00:39:06,400
What are you doing?

938
00:39:04,310 --> 00:39:06,210
[Entrance]

939
00:39:10,480 --> 00:39:11,740
Why are you getting up?

940
00:39:11,760 --> 00:39:12,840
Just lie down.

941
00:39:13,510 --> 00:39:14,670
I'm not used to this.

942
00:39:15,880 --> 00:39:16,800
You just got here.

943
00:39:16,800 --> 00:39:17,590
It's normal

944
00:39:17,590 --> 00:39:19,190
to feel a little out of place.

945
00:39:19,360 --> 00:39:20,190
Tonight, I'd like to

946
00:39:20,190 --> 00:39:21,150
buy you a couple of drinks.

947
00:39:21,150 --> 00:39:22,840
Let me give you a proper welcome.

948
00:39:22,840 --> 00:39:23,760
Then I'll tell you all about

949
00:39:23,760 --> 00:39:25,420
how things work at Xiaoximen.

950
00:39:26,150 --> 00:39:27,190
I don't drink.

951
00:39:29,230 --> 00:39:30,760
I couldn't drink at first either.

952
00:39:30,760 --> 00:39:32,030
After a few times, I got used to it.

953
00:39:32,030 --> 00:39:33,800
I trained Zhang to hold his liquor.

954
00:39:33,800 --> 00:39:34,510
Zhang.

955
00:39:34,510 --> 00:39:35,590
Zhang. Zhang.

956
00:39:36,630 --> 00:39:38,160
Let's go drinking tonight.

957
00:39:41,840 --> 00:39:43,400
I've got plans tonight.

958
00:39:43,760 --> 00:39:44,710
I'll pass.

959
00:39:45,000 --> 00:39:46,190
What plans?

960
00:39:46,280 --> 00:39:47,800
Maybe next time.

961
00:39:48,400 --> 00:39:50,660
There's a patient in emergency surgery.

962
00:39:59,000 --> 00:40:00,000
Dr. Liu,

963
00:40:00,000 --> 00:40:00,630
why don't you go?

964
00:40:00,630 --> 00:40:02,890
It'll be a good chance to learn the ropes.

965
00:40:20,710 --> 00:40:23,510
I thought we'd finally got
someone who could work.

966
00:40:28,440 --> 00:40:30,320
[Xiaoximen Hospital; Name: Liu Zhengliang]

967
00:40:32,590 --> 00:40:34,360
We're screwed. It's Duan.

968
00:40:36,550 --> 00:40:37,280
What do we do?

969
00:40:38,320 --> 00:40:39,050
What do we do?

970
00:40:40,000 --> 00:40:42,230
Should I go?

971
00:40:43,480 --> 00:40:44,510
If it's Duan,

972
00:40:44,510 --> 00:40:46,320
it's just a formality anyway.

973
00:40:46,320 --> 00:40:47,320
It makes no difference who goes.

974
00:40:47,320 --> 00:40:49,190
What are you talking about?
I went last time.

975
00:40:49,190 --> 00:40:50,110
No, no, don't do that.

976
00:40:50,110 --> 00:40:52,070
You just said you'd go.

977
00:40:52,190 --> 00:40:53,120
Come on, enough.

978
00:40:59,630 --> 00:41:00,710
Who's Duan?

979
00:41:01,230 --> 00:41:03,030
My mom has this pain
on the right side of her lower back.

980
00:41:03,030 --> 00:41:04,230
It comes in waves

981
00:41:04,320 --> 00:41:05,630
and shoots downward.

982
00:41:06,280 --> 00:41:08,480
It's so bad she can barely straighten up.

983
00:41:08,480 --> 00:41:10,320
Do you also feel bloated
in your lower abdomen?

984
00:41:10,320 --> 00:41:11,550
Her lower abdomen is bloated too.

985
00:41:11,550 --> 00:41:12,630
She took painkillers,

986
00:41:12,630 --> 00:41:13,670
but they didn't help.

987
00:41:13,670 --> 00:41:15,670
Now she's running a high fever

988
00:41:15,670 --> 00:41:17,000
and shivering.

989
00:41:17,000 --> 00:41:18,000
Please give her a proper examination.

990
00:41:18,000 --> 00:41:19,730
What's wrong with her, Doctor?

991
00:41:19,920 --> 00:41:21,480
Let's run a few tests first.

992
00:41:21,480 --> 00:41:22,810
I'm not doing any tests.

993
00:41:25,360 --> 00:41:26,320
Director Duan,

994
00:41:26,070 --> 00:41:30,490
[Emergency Room 18]

995
00:41:26,320 --> 00:41:27,360
if you won't get checked,

996
00:41:27,360 --> 00:41:29,820
how am I supposed
to figure out what's wrong?

997
00:41:35,550 --> 00:41:36,800
Why not just put me

998
00:41:36,800 --> 00:41:37,960
on an IV?

999
00:41:37,960 --> 00:41:40,360
How can I give you an IV
without examining you first?

1000
00:41:40,360 --> 00:41:42,360
At least get a complete blood count.

1001
00:41:42,440 --> 00:41:43,360
It only costs a few dozen yuan.

1002
00:41:43,360 --> 00:41:44,510
That's cheaper than at a big hospital.

1003
00:41:44,510 --> 00:41:45,880
No way.

1004
00:41:45,880 --> 00:41:48,110
I've got a ton of things waiting for me.

1005
00:41:48,110 --> 00:41:48,920
But you...

1006
00:41:48,920 --> 00:41:49,360
If you won't get checked,

1007
00:41:49,360 --> 00:41:51,280
I can't prescribe anything either.

1008
00:41:51,280 --> 00:41:52,320
Let's run a test.

1009
00:41:53,030 --> 00:41:54,290
Yeah, let's run a test.

1010
00:41:54,400 --> 00:41:55,440
Right, let's run one.

1011
00:41:55,440 --> 00:41:56,030
Let's run one, okay?

1012
00:41:56,030 --> 00:41:58,030
All right, I'm putting in the order.

1013
00:41:58,110 --> 00:41:59,030
We're already here.

1014
00:41:59,030 --> 00:42:01,090
Come on. Let's just get one test done.

1015
00:42:06,000 --> 00:42:07,960
She has pain in her right lower back,

1016
00:42:07,960 --> 00:42:09,290
with chills and a fever.

1017
00:42:09,800 --> 00:42:10,880
Most likely,

1018
00:42:10,880 --> 00:42:12,920
it's a ureteral stone with an infection.

1019
00:42:12,920 --> 00:42:13,880
Anyway, after a lot of persuading,

1020
00:42:13,880 --> 00:42:15,190
I got her to agree to a blood test.

1021
00:42:15,190 --> 00:42:15,670
There's a good chance

1022
00:42:15,670 --> 00:42:17,670
she'll still need an ultrasound later.

1023
00:42:17,670 --> 00:42:18,590
But the moment I suggest it,

1024
00:42:18,590 --> 00:42:20,150
she'll definitely give me a hard time.

1025
00:42:20,150 --> 00:42:21,810
Can you two go talk her into it?

1026
00:42:25,620 --> 00:42:28,010
[Interpreting Treatise on the Spleen and
Stomach Through Five Circuits and Six Qi]

1027
00:42:28,920 --> 00:42:29,710
Huang.

1028
00:42:29,590 --> 00:42:31,980
[Interpreting Treatise on the Spleen and
Stomach Through Five Circuits and Six Qi]

1029
00:42:30,440 --> 00:42:32,070
Why don't you go?

1030
00:42:32,430 --> 00:42:33,540
I'll buy you drinks tonight.

1031
00:42:33,540 --> 00:42:37,980
[Interpreting Treatise on the Spleen and
Stomach Through Five Circuits and Six Qi]

1032
00:42:34,030 --> 00:42:35,190
No need. You...

1033
00:42:35,190 --> 00:42:36,400
Didn't you say you weren't going?

1034
00:42:36,400 --> 00:42:39,060
I already made plans
with... with someone else.

1035
00:42:45,320 --> 00:42:46,720
Why don't you skip it too?

1036
00:42:46,960 --> 00:42:48,110
The four of us are a team, anyway.

1037
00:42:48,110 --> 00:42:50,440
Worst case, we all get punished together.

1038
00:42:54,400 --> 00:42:56,400
What... What kind of attitude is that?
